# Balanced native strong-baseline cost calibration

Prospective 2026-10-12 after source build and native normalization diagnostic; no timings for these data inspected. Same active idea/revision and fixed runtime. This batch asks whether permutation-stage optimization can materially accelerate current native CTT and whether ordinary RFF is an adequate simple cost comparator. It does NOT estimate power, Type-I error, or establish a new method.

Primary source: pinned goodpoints CTT paper Section5/AppendixH and author test.py; pinned Cheap Permutation tests/util_sqMMD_estimators_cheap.py cheap_perm/cheap_rff and native Gaussian generator. Source digests in native_build_manifest_v2.json. Cheap's complete permutation comparator is cheap_perm(s=n), not its confusingly named legacy complete Rademacher routine. Six arms: unchanged CTT g=0 and g=1 s=16; exact Gaussian complete permutation s=n; Cheap Permutation s=16; ordinary author RFF r=128; Cheap RFF r=128,s=16 (existing optimized binned feature baseline). Common B=39, alpha=.05, float64, same inputs and null/statistic seeds. Counts balanced, so prior unequal-count discrepancy is avoided; CTT score is positive-rescaled and cannot be compared numerically to raw MMD across g. For ordinary versus Cheap RFF original-data feature MMD must match within1e-10; complete versus Cheap exact original-data MMD must match within1e-10. Their permutation null distributions differ and need not match.

Native Gaussian generator, d=10, mean_diff=.06 (means +/- .03 in last coordinate), n per group in {1024,4096}; these reduced sizes intentionally calibrate compute/state, not reproduce n=16384 reported power. At each n use three independent data seeds 930,931,932; pair methods within each dataset. Preserve arrays or exact native generator+seed hash. Fit lambda using author's sqrt(2)*median pooled Euclidean distance rule on first512 observations of an independent seed10 sample; charge data generation and bandwidth time once per dataset and report arm+shared setup as well as kernel path only. The same seed10 for both sizes generates different second-group offsets as native n changes, disclose that; no outcome-driven bandwidth selection. One unmeasured tiny n=64 warmup per arm is charged in batch wall time; all36 measured arm runs retained. Deterministically shuffle arm order using seed1212+n+data_seed. No subagent numeric tasks; single-thread CPU. Shared host contention is observed/unknown, no fair exclusive-host claim.

Measure full wall/core-seconds and native per-call total; nonoverlapping compression, Gaussian kernel construction, feature construction, permutation signed-sum, feature Gram and remaining time via transparent call-through wrappers. Data generation/bandwidth outside kernel timers. Process ru_maxrss is cumulative batch high-water, not per-arm attribution. Also report exact array state sizes from native shapes. Preserve native score arrays and rejects as diagnostics only; three trials cannot estimate level/power. Mean across paired data units per n for time/fraction; ranges and individual values retained, no significance claims. Cost-ranking alone does not establish statistical domination.

Hypothesis/prediction: s=16 CTT permutation arithmetic is small vs compression, so removing it entirely cannot produce a20% end-to-end reduction at these sizes. Falsifier: measured nonoverlapping signed-sum arithmetic consistently exceeds20% full path; inconclusive if interference makes scope unclear. This tests only that component, not all possible early stopping or changes to compression. Baseline contrast: Cheap RFF avoids ordinary RFF's full 2n*r stored feature matrix and reduces permutation arithmetic; its feature-generation cost persists. Use measured component fraction p to report optimistic1/(1-p), conditional on remaining work unchanged. If hypothesis supported, do not develop permutation-arithmetic-only CTT optimization; continue strongest comparator/quality/source audit, including Nyström protocol, before selecting a genuinely distinct mechanism. If refuted, inspect call/overhead profile before designing any change. No replacement method authored here.

